[[4564,1723,"no one was taking responsibility for his care in a 'key worker' type role","lack of key worker",""],[4565,1723,"risk assessments themselves were therefore superficial, often relying uncritically on self-reporting without meaningfully engaging in suicide risk prevention","superficial risk assessments",""],[4566,1723,"failure to meaningfully communicate and engage with his Regiment and the medical staff attached to it","lack of communication with armed forces",""],[4567,1723,"Communication with the family was superficial and the evidence was that their perception was that they couldn't fully share issues and concerns because of perceived barriers in information sharing","superficial family communication",""],[4568,1723,"staff in the team struggled with decision making around information sharing","inadequate risk sharing",""],[8214,3140,"The ambulance service was called at 2049 on 14 November 2022 and the call was graded as a Category 2 call requiring a response within 40 minutes. The ambulance finally arrived at 0044 on 15 November 2022","delayed ambulance arrival",""],[8215,3140,"YAS were not resourced to respond to the number of emergency calls","insufficient ambulance resources",""],[8216,3140,"There was a significant delay in offloading patients at hospitals which tied up ambulance resource and meant they were unable to respond to emergency calls","delayed patient offloading",""]]